//? Title: Shannon–Fano partitions: actual split choices and Huffman comparison
//? Subtitle: Actual canonical histories, retained original fixtures and explicit controls
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Build a byte prefix code by repeatedly splitting a frequency-ordered alphabet
into two groups with nearly equal total counts. Actual native choices precede
the original85-byte pangram comparison with empirical entropy, Huffman and
the8-bit baseline.
)

\toc

> Mechanism and mathematical scope

Sort symbols by decreasing frequency. At each nonleaf range choose the earliest
split minimizing absolute left-minus-right weight, append0 to left words and1 to
right words, then recurse. Distinct leaves separate at a split, proving
prefix-freeness. This greedy top-down choice need not minimize weighted path
length; Huffman supplies the optimal binary prefix-code comparison under the
stated symbol model. Empty input has no words and zero average; a singleton uses
one bit. Native construction counters measure actual candidate boundary tests
and word-bit appends. Encoding and decoding use the checked complete-payload
trie shared with the midpoint-code implementation.

> A tiny actual producing history

The table and native concept diagram read the same producing execution. Every
block below is a complete editable C++ program.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/shannon_fano_tiny.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
    namespace a = dm::algorithms;
    namespace g = dm::graphics;
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    auto r = a::shannon_fano_build_trace("aaaabbc");
    std::print("Actual sorted byte ids `{}`, counts `{}`.\n\n| begin | end | actual split | left count | " "right count | imbalance |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n",
               r.sorted_symbols, r.sorted_frequencies);
    for (const auto &s : r.splits)
        std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n", s.begin, s.end,
                   s.middle, s.left, s.right, s.imbalance);
    g::Diagram concept_diagram(48, 1100);
    concept_diagram.node("n0", {0, 0}, "Byte counts4,2,1");
    concept_diagram.node("n1", {5, 0},
                         std::format("Actual split decisions {}",
                                     r.splits.size()));
    concept_diagram.node("n2", {10, 0},
                         std::format("Actual weighted payload bits {}",
                                     r.weighted_bits));
    concept_diagram.edge("n0", "n1").edge("n1", "n2");
    concept_diagram.save_svg("build/shannon_fano_tiny.svg");
}
```
